// experiments/exp_coulomb.ddk — recover the fine-structure constant from the
// single soliton's near-field Coulomb tail.
//
// Method: build one centered soliton, evaluate its energy-density field, and measure
// E_out(R) (energy outside radius R). On the Coulomb plateau E_out(R)*R is constant
// and equals alpha_sol*hbar c/2, giving alpha_sol^-1 = hbar c / (2 E_out(R) R).
// The interaction of two such opposite charges then follows: V(d) = -alpha_sol hbar c / d.
//
// Scope note: this recovers alpha to ~10% (order of magnitude of CODATA 137.036).
// The precise value and the running of alpha require the paper's full dipole
// minimization at large separation, which is beyond this teaching reproduction.
use constants
use field
use energy
use coulomb

f = centered_soliton()
dens = energy_density(f[0], f[1], f[2], f[3])
rfield = center_radius()

print("R [fm] | E_out*R [MeV*fm] (target 0.720) | alpha_sol^-1 (CODATA 137.036)")
print(2.0)
print(coulomb_coeff(dens, rfield, 2.0))
print(alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 2.0))
print(2.5)
print(coulomb_coeff(dens, rfield, 2.5))
print(alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 2.5))
print(3.0)
print(coulomb_coeff(dens, rfield, 3.0))
print(alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 3.0))
print(3.5)
print(coulomb_coeff(dens, rfield, 3.5))
print(alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 3.5))
print(4.0)
print(coulomb_coeff(dens, rfield, 4.0))
print(alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 4.0))

// Plateau average over the near-field window R = 2.0 .. 4.0 fm.
a1 = alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 2.0)
a2 = alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 2.5)
a3 = alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 3.0)
a4 = alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 3.5)
a5 = alpha_inv_at(dens, rfield, 4.0)
amean = (a1 + a2 + a3 + a4 + a5) / 5.0
print("near-field mean alpha_sol^-1:")
print(amean)
